What is Cloud Identity and Access Management?
Cloud Identity and Access Management (CIAM) is a suite of technologies that provide centralized control over user identities and access permissions across heterogeneous environments, including public clouds, private data centers, and edge devices. By consolidating authentication, authorization, and lifecycle management, CIAM platforms reduce administrative overhead, enhance security posture, and support compliance with evolving data privacy regulations.
